#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""wiki-traits — cross-test the personality profile against the whole corpus.

Pure stdlib. Reuses `psychometrics`' PREDICTIONS table, `wiki-lexicon`'s four
corpus readers and `mine-tweets`' archive loader, so every trap those files
document is handled once and not re-solved here.

WHY THIS EXISTS
---------------
`SYNTHESIS_SPEC.md`'s constitution pass makes the cognitive stack register 1
and the measured personality profile register 2 — the first two things every
synthesis must be checked against. Both registers currently point at *pages*.
A page states a score; it does not say how much weight a conclusion may put on
it. So the pass can be run honestly and still lean the whole argument on a
trait the corpus has never corroborated, which is what a register that names a
file rather than a measurement permits.

This computes the missing number, on two axes that must never be added
together.

  SUPPORT  (Tier A)  how much of Dan's own behavioural output carries the trait
  REACH    (Tier C)  how much of the wiki's own reasoning already leans on it

THE CIRCULARITY, WHICH IS THE WHOLE REASON FOR THE TIERS
--------------------------------------------------------
The obvious build — "test each trait against everything, raw and wiki alike,
and score it" — produces a confidently circular number, and it would look like
the strongest evidence in the repository.

Measured on 2026-09-06: **122 of 483 pages carry personality vocabulary, and 38
of 61 synthesis pages do.** Those pages were written by agents that had read
`wiki/mind/profile/`. A trait scored across them is not being tested against
the corpus; it is being tested against how often the writing process reached
for its vocabulary. `intp` is cited by 46 pages. Every one of those citations
is downstream of the claim, not evidence for it.

So the corpus is stratified by whether a source could have been contaminated by
the profile pages, and only one tier may confirm anything:

  Tier A — behavioural, uncontaminated. First-party text Dan produced without
           knowing what the wiki would say: sent messages, tweets, his own
           turns in AI transcripts. **The only tier that is evidence.**
  Tier B — first-person testimony. The instrument scores themselves, and
           `context-core`. This is the CLAIM, not support for it. Its standing
           is the testimony ledger's, currently 57/100 over n=14.
  Tier C — wiki-derived. Measures REACH: how load-bearing the trait already is
           in the corpus's own reasoning. Reach is never support. A trait can
           have enormous reach and no evidence, and that combination is the
           single most dangerous object this system can hold.

WHAT THE TWO AXES PRODUCE
-------------------------
The output is a quadrant, not a ranking, and the useful cells are the off-
diagonal ones:

  supported + load-bearing  → earned. The wiki reasons from a measured thing.
  supported + dormant       → UNDERUSED. A measured mechanism the wiki is not
                              reasoning from. This is exactly the failure
                              SYNTHESIS_SPEC's worked example documents: three
                              synthesis pages on cognition cited one of the
                              eleven profile pages between them.
  silent    + load-bearing  → UNSUPPORTED LOAD. Every page in the reach set is
                              reasoning from a premise nothing measured. This
                              is the quadrant the tool exists to surface.
  silent    + dormant       → fine. Noted, not chased.

THE ASYMMETRY, INHERITED AND NON-NEGOTIABLE
-------------------------------------------
From `psychometrics`, and it governs every number below:

    failure to corroborate is not falsification.

Three of four core axioms tested lexically were invisible, *time = countdown*
the clearest negative. A trait can be real and leave no lexical trace, because
people do not narrate their own architecture in text messages. So `silent`
means THE CORPUS DOES NOT CARRY THIS — never "the trait is absent" — and its
consequence is about how much weight a synthesis may place on it, never about
whether it is true. Only an INVERTED result is evidence against a score.

There is therefore no confidence percentage anywhere in this tool, and one must
never be added. A percentage needs a denominator of things that could have
disconfirmed, and silence is not one of them. Bands, and their counts.

THE CONTROL PROBLEM ACROSS REGISTERS
------------------------------------
Only the message corpus has a within-medium control — 110,944 messages received
from 503 handles. There is no such thing as a received tweet or a received
prompt, so a raw rate in the other three registers is uninterpretable on its
own, which is the trap `psychometrics` documents in its first paragraph.

So the registers are not scored the same way and their numbers are never
pooled:

  messages         → ratio against the control → a verdict
  twitter/ai       → rank of the proxy WITHIN that register against all other
                     proxies → replication, not verdict

A trait replicates when it lands in the upper half of its register's own proxy
ranking. Replication across registers is the control-free evidence that a trait
is dispositional rather than an artefact of one medium.

WHAT IS NOT READ, AND WHY
-------------------------
**Facebook.** 286 MB and 1,686 HTML files, and the export is nested inside
itself — `facebook-ihatedanfrank/facebook-ihatedanfrank/` holds a second copy
of `posts/your_posts_1.html`. Counting the tree as it stands double-counts
every post. No reader in `bin/` handles it and writing one is its own job with
its own trap. It is a real fifth register and its absence is a stated gap, not
an oversight.

USAGE
  bin/wiki-traits support            Tier A: every trait across four registers
  bin/wiki-traits reach              Tier C: the wiki's own footprint per trait
  bin/wiki-traits map                the quadrant — the filter output
  bin/wiki-traits assess ti_dominance   what weight a synthesis may put on it
  bin/wiki-traits review             the proxy review queue
  bin/wiki-traits mine               recompute traits/measured.json (~90s)
  bin/wiki-traits page               regenerate the wiki entry
  bin/wiki-traits check              the gate
"""
import argparse
import json
import os
import re
import sys
from collections import Counter
from importlib.machinery import SourceFileLoader

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
MEASURED = os.path.join(ROOT, "traits", "measured.json")
PAGE = os.path.join(ROOT, "wiki", "mind", "profile", "trait-corpus-map.md")

# A trait must land in the top quarter of a register's own proxy ranking, on a
# non-trivial number of hits, to count as replicated there. The first build used
# the median and it was meaningless by construction: half of all proxies clear a
# median, so every trait "replicated in all three registers" and the column
# carried no information at all.
REPLICATION_QUANTILE = 0.75
REPLICATION_MIN_HITS = 10

# Reach bands, in pages out of the 483 non-index entries. A trait cited by
# thirty-odd pages is structural in this corpus; one cited by under five is
# not being reasoned from.
REACH_LOAD_BEARING = 20
REACH_PRESENT = 5


def _mod(name, fname):
    return SourceFileLoader(name, os.path.join(ROOT, "bin", fname)).load_module()


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The trait registry.
#
# `facets` are the keys in psychometrics.PREDICTIONS this trait owns.
# `wiki` is how the trait shows up in wiki PROSE, which is a different string
# problem from how it shows up in a text message — `Ti` is a cognitive
# function in one and a typo in the other, so the wiki pattern is anchored on
# vocabulary the profile pages actually established.
# `register` is the constitution-pass register this trait feeds.
#
# A `wiki` pattern is held to the same standard as a Tier A proxy and was
# checked the same way. Three were broken on the first run and each inflated a
# reach count enough to change a cell:
#   liberalism   `left` matched "**Checked, left standing**" — constitution-pass
#                boilerplate present on every synthesis page — plus "left the
#                company" and "2020 left turn". 202 pages, almost all spurious.
#   sociability  `withdraw` matched "troop withdrawal" and "was withdrawn".
#   anxiety      bare `worry` more than doubled the count over `anxiet|anxious`.
# Reach is not evidence, but an inflated reach count moves a trait into a
# louder cell and manufactures an obligation, so it is checked like one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
